      "writtenOn": "2026-03-27T23:01:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hey Ryan, I noticed your CL, and thought it looked familiar :). I introduced a similar feature for SVT-AV1, by extending the CRF range from 63 to 70: https://gitlab.com/AOMediaCodec/SVT-AV1/-/merge_requests/2522\n\nI\u0027m not sure how much time you want to spend at optimizing the quality at this very low range, but I\u0027ve found a few things during the development of the SVT-AV1 equivalent that helped with subjective quality:\n1. Compressing frame qindex scaling across the frame hierarchy performed better than clamping qindex (the latter caused big quality fluctuations across frames)\n2. Scaling rdmults to bias toward further bitrate savings also helped\n3. Leaving a bit of frame scaling was beneficial rather than completely shutting it off (every frame is encoded at qindex 255)",
      "parentUuid": "0abc740d_b948471b",
      "revId": "98ce4f15eb68c6de02d8bf5f0b106e418291067b",
